From: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Subject: KVM: s390: pci: Fix GISC refcount leak on AIF enable failure
Patch-mainline: v7.2-rc4
Git-commit: 7b69729046a4c58f4cb457184e5ac4aaa179bff4
References: bsc#1277451

Description: KVM/s390/pci: Fix resource leaks and cleanup in error paths
Symptom: resource leaks, denial-of-service
Problem: Error paths in interrupt forwarding logic for passthrough PCI devices
         failed to cleanup resources correctly.       
Solution: Fix the logic and handle cleanup appropriately.      
Reproduction:  -

Upstream-Description:

              KVM: s390: pci: Fix GISC refcount leak on AIF enable failure

              kvm_s390_gisc_register() registers the guest ISC before pinning
              the guest interrupt forwarding pages and allocating the AISB bit.
              If any of the later setup steps fails, the function unwinds the
              pinned pages and other local state, but does not unregister the
              GISC reference. Add the missing kvm_s390_gisc_unregister() to the
              error unwind path.

              Fixes: 3c5a1b6f0a18 ("KVM: s390: pci: provide routines for enabling/disabling interrupt forwarding")
              Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
              Signed-off-by: Haoxiang Li <haoxiang_li2024@163.com>
              Reviewed-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
              Tested-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
              Acked-by: Claudio Imbrenda <imbrenda@linux.ibm.com>
              Reviewed-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>
              Signed-off-by: Claudio Imbrenda <imbrenda@linux.ibm.com>
              Message-ID: <20260624061910.2794734-1-haoxiang_li2024@163.com>
              Signed-off-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>


Signed-off-by: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Acked-by: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
---
 arch/s390/kvm/pci.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
+++ b/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
@@ -330,6 +330,7 @@ unpin2:
 unpin1:
 	unpin_user_page(aibv_page);
 out:
+	kvm_s390_gisc_unregister(kvm, fib->fmt0.isc);
 	return rc;
 }
 
